RF.put("questb:b53",{"8693":{"id":8693,"t":"Cloak of Veiled Shadows","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Martial Drape, 2 Azure Idols, 5 Bronze Scarabs and 5 Ivory Scarabs to Keyl Swiftclaw in Silithus. You must also obtain Revered reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Martial Drape General Rajaxx 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Kurinnaxx 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ayamiss the Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Buru the Gorger 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\n2 Azure Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 21000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"I'm glad to hear you're aiding us in our attack on Ahn'Qiraj, ‹name›. I can make you a protective item that'll be of assistance in the fight against our enemy, ‹class›.\nI shall need a Qiraji drape, which I'll resize for you of course. I'll also need idols and scarabs which I'll use to create a suitable clasp.\nI promise you won't be disappointed.","rew":"You will receive:\nCloak of Veiled Shadows\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring the materials for the cloak, ‹name›?","done":"Ah yes... this drape is immaculate.\nTake this cloak, ‹name›. May it protect you from the foul magic of the Qiraji.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.8,"y":39.5,"n":"Keyl Swiftclaw","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8853":{"id":8853,"t":"Fifteen Signets for War Supplies","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"15 Horde Commendation Signet","rew":"You will receive:\nAhn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":29.8,"y":67.3,"n":"Warlord Gorchuk","s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8533":{"id":8533,"t":"The Horde Needs More Copper Bars!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 copper bars to Miner Cromwell in Durotar.\n20 Copper Bar","desc":"Back so soon? You'll be a real miner in no time ‹class›. So, you already know the drill; I need you to go out, mine up a mess of copper ore, smelt it into bars and bring it back to me here. I know that's something you're capable of, the question is, are you willing?","rew":"You will receive:\nHorde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Back so soon? You'll be a real miner in no time, ‹class›. So, you already know the drill; I need you to go out, mine up a mess of copper ore, smelt it into bars and bring it back to me here. I know that's something you're capable of, the question is, are you willing?","done":"You've proven yourself to me yet again, ‹class›. I will see to it that this copper is used in due time. For now though, I need to get these copper bars onto the pallet and tallied. If you still feel inclined, I could probably use your help in gathering even more copper bars.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.6,"y":66.7,"n":"Miner Cromwell","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"8613":{"id":8613,"t":"The Horde Needs Spotted Yellowtail!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 1 instead of 52.","obj":"Bring 20 Spotted Yellowtail to Fisherman Lin'do at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Spotted Yellowtail Raene Wolfrunner 0.7 % , Volcor 0.7 % , Terenthis 0.7 % , Sentinel Selarin 0.7 % and 4 more","desc":"It be a nice day for fishin', don't'cha think mon? Good thing, cuz I be needin' a lot of fish it lookin' like. The Horde, they askin' me to be in charge of collectin' a ton of the spotted yellowtail for them. They say they needin' it for the war they getting' ready for at Ahn'Qiraj. I say to them I do the best I can. So I be needin' to get some help. You gonna be helpin' me, ‹class›?","rew":"You will receive:\n10 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","back":"Back so soon with the spotted yellowtail, ‹class›? You rememba' to cook it up nice? We not servin' raw fish to the soldiers out in the hot desert sun, to be sure.","done":"Oh ya, this be the good stuff. I pack it up real nice so it not go to waste. Thanks be to you for helpin' me out like this. I'm thinkin' you an A-number-one fisherman for all this spotted yellowtail. An if you happen to fish up and cook even more, you bring it to me here; I make sure everyone know you did!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":29.1,"y":68.9,"n":"Fisherman Lin'do","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"5893":{"id":5893,"t":"Coldtooth Supplies","lv":55,"min":51,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 55 instead of 60. Pays 40s instead of 0.","obj":"Bring 10 Coldtooth Supplies to the Horde Quatermaster in Frostwolf Keep.\n10 Coldtooth Supplies Coldtooth Supplies in Alterac Valley","desc":"The Coldtooth mine to the north was once an ideal place to store extra supplies, but now that the fighting with the Stormpikes grows fierce, we do not always have the spare warriors to station at the mine and protect it. And so, control of the mine often falls to the Alliance, or to underground denizens...\nBut we still need our supplies, ‹name›! Go to the Coldtooth mine and bring me a load of them. And be wary of enemies as you go; the tides of battle shift quickly in that place...","rew":"Money: 40 0 gold, 40 silver, 0 copper\n+25 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Have you been to the Coldtooth mine, ‹name›? Do you have the supplies I asked for?","done":"Ah, you got them. Good work, ‹name›! These supplies are a little musty from sitting in that dark mine for so long, but we'll make use of them nonetheless.\nThank you, ‹name›. Your deeds are vital to the maintenance of our fighting forces.\nStart Frostwolf Quartermaster Alterac Valley End Frostwolf Quartermaster Alterac Valley Level 55 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 53 58 Side Horde Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 5893","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"693":{"id":693,"t":"Wand over Fist","lv":39,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Trelane's Wand of Invocation and return it to Skuerto at Refuge Pointe.\nTrelane's Wand of Invocation Kor'gresh Coldrage","desc":"Hey, ‹name›. Sorry to be so short with ye earlier... and no, that ain't a pun.\nI figured out where Trelane's first item ended up: Kor'gresh has it in Boulderfist Hall. An' by the way he was throwing down blasts of ice at his kin to keep them in line, he must be close to figurin' out how to use all of its powers.\nBoulderfist Hall's south of here an' then east of Thandol Span. Find the ogre an' get back that wand.\nWhile you're gone, I'll figure out what we're gonna do about Stromgarde.","rew":"Experience: 3,000\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Our goal is the wand, ‹name›. Focus on that for now.","done":"Brilliant, ‹name›. One item down an' three more to go, based on my list. The other three items are all in Stromgarde.\nTake a rest an' get your strength back--the next phase of my plan'll require a little more time an' effort. Come back to me after you've gotten a warm meal an' some rest.","pins":[{"z":"Arathi Highlands","x":46.7,"y":47,"n":"Skuerto","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["arathi-highlands"]},"4133":{"id":4133,"t":"Vivian Lagrave","lv":55,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Shadowmaster Vivian Lagrave in Kargath.","desc":"Shadowmaster Vivian Lagrave is in need of your services. She is in the Badlands, in the orcish outpost of Kargath, pursuing rumors of a certain brew made by the Dark Iron dwarves of Blackrock Depths.\nSpeak with Vivian. She awaits you.","rew":"Experience: 550","done":"Thank you for coming, ‹name›. This place is not without a stark charm, but is lacks the amenities of the Apothecarium.\nEnough with the pleasantries. To business, yes?\nUndercity Badlands","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":50.1,"y":68,"n":"Apothecary Zinge","s":1},{"z":"Badlands","x":2.9,"y":47.8,"n":"Shadowmage Vivian Lagrave","e":1}],"cats":["blackrock-depths"]},"2773":{"id":2773,"t":"The Mithril Kid","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring two Heavy Mithril Breastplates and one Ornate Mithril Gloves to Trenton Lighthammer.\n2 Heavy Mithril Breastplate\nOrnate Mithril Gloves","desc":"Around these parts I am known as the Mithril Kid. I supply ornate mithril to adventurers from around the world.\n<Trenton whispers.>\nLittle do they know that I do not know the technique to fashion ornate mithril gloves. Shhhh! This will be our little secret.\nTeach me the technique to create ornate mithril gloves, ‹name›, and in exchange, I will show you the resultant of the culmination of my training under Galvan: the ornate mithril breastplate.","rew":"You will learn: Ornate Mithril Breastplate\nExperience: 3,900","back":"Have you completed the crafting of the items, ‹name›?","done":"Thank you for all that you have taught me, ‹name›. The master and commander of the ornate mithril set will soon be in your possession.\nBehold!","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.4,"y":28.8,"n":"Trenton Lighthammer","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"7653":{"id":7653,"t":"Imperial Plate Belt","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"20 Thorium Bar","rew":"You will receive:\nPlans: Imperial Plate Belt\n+100 reputation with Thorium Brotherhood","back":"For the belt plans, I'll be needin' 20 thorium bars.","done":"A pleasure doin' business with ya.\nAnd ‹name›, wipe that look of disgust off yer face.","pins":[{"z":"Tanaris","x":51.4,"y":28.7,"n":"Derotain Mudsipper","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blacksmithing"]},"97973":{"id":97973,"t":"Camping 101 tailoring","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Taleen Shimmerthread in Shen'dar Village to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your tailoring skill to 20","desc":"Tailoring is a surprisingly potent tradeskill to invest in, and I'm sure it'll serve you well.\nI know someone that can teach you how to craft a Faction Banner for your camp, provided you have the skill for it. Inspiration and morale are a key part of success on any battlefield, and an inspirational banner can go a long way to keeping you energized.","done":"There you have it, you can now craft your very own Rallying Banner. Most folk don't care much for camps being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":41.6,"y":44.8,"n":"Raan Wildwind","s":1},{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":44.8,"y":44.2,"n":"Taleen Shimmerthread","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94293":{"id":94293,"t":"Craftsmans writ guardian cloak","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Guardian Cloak\nGuardian Cloak","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Guardian Cloak, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Guardian Cloak Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94293","cats":["crafting"]},"94213":{"id":94213,"t":"Craftsmans writ lesser mana potion","min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet. Partly read from what players of our addon saw in game.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Lesser Mana Potion\nLesser Mana Potion","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting 1 Lesser Mana Potion, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin Pouch\n+75 reputation with Azeroth Commerce Authority\n+75 reputation with Durotar Supply and Logistics","back":"Good day, ‹race›. I appreciate the company but my attention is elsewhere. If we do not have business, please be on your way.","done":"Ah, is this the potion I requested?\n<The elven woman respectfully takes the vial from you.>\nYour arrival is timely, and your generosity deeply appreciated. I accept this, and offer you a small token of my gratitude.\nThank you, may we meet again.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":60.3,"y":72.6,"n":"Ash'alari","e":1}],"cats":["crafting"]},"7893":{"id":7893,"t":"Rituals of Strength","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"8 Dense Grinding Stone","rew":"You will receive:\n20 Darkmoon Faire Prize Ticket\n+100 reputation with Darkmoon Faire","back":"‹name›, in my quest to become the strongest woman alive, I have traveled the world and learned muscle building secrets from distant weight masters, strength gurus, and ancient manuals. I now know forbidden exercises that would kill the weak and cripple the uninitiated!\nThese feats of strength and conditioning require training with the densest of grinding stones. ‹name›, can you find or make some grinding stones and bring them to me? I'll give you tickets if you do...","done":"Thanks much, ‹name›. Here's your Darkmoon Faire tickets!\nMulgore Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":38.6,"y":46.4,"n":"Kerri Hicks","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":40.5,"y":69.9,"n":"Kerri Hicks","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"453":{"id":453,"t":"Finding the Shadowy Figure","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Shadowy Figure. Your clues:\nHe is not native to Darkshire.\nHe is a nervous, jittery person.\nHe left Darkshire and headed west.\nBook from Sven's Farm\nProvided: Book from Sven's Farm","desc":"Good luck, ‹name›. I hope you find the chap, and I hope you find him alive.\nIf he's left the safety of Darkshire then he could be prey to the beasts of the wilds.","rew":"Experience: 1,000\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Who are you?? Leave me be!","done":"<Jitters sighs...>\nYes, I'm the author of that book. You finally found me, eh?\nWell if you read that journal...then you only know the half of it!","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":73.8,"y":44.5,"n":"Tavernkeep Smitts","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":18.4,"y":56.4,"n":"Jitters","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"133":{"id":133,"t":"Ghoulish Effigy","lv":27,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather 7 Ghoul Ribs and bring them to Abercrombie at his shack.\n7 Ghoul Rib Rotted One 80 % , Plague Spreader 80 % , Brain Eater 80 % , Bone Chewer 80 % and 1 more","desc":"I live so far from the protection of town, it's a wonder the ghouls and the walking dead haven't eaten me! In fact, just yesterday a pack of Bone Chewers was pounding on the walls of my house!\nI want to make an effigy - a kind of \"scarecrow\" for Ghouls. To do that I need some Ghoul Ribs. You can get them from Flesh Eaters, Bone Chewers, Brain Eaters, Rotted Ones and Plague Spreaders.\nGet the ribs for me, and I will repay you with some coin.","rew":"Money: 22 0 gold, 22 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,650","back":"I think I hear a pack of Ghouls scurrying around the back of the house - I better put that effigy up quick! Did you get those Ghoul Ribs for me?","done":"Ah, thanks. These will do just the trick!","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":28.1,"y":31.5,"n":"Abercrombie","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"1253":{"id":1253,"t":"The Black Shield","lv":35,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Blackened Iron Shield to Captain Garran Vimes in Theramore.\nBlackened Iron Shield\nProvided: Blackened Iron Shield","desc":"An iron shield, blackened by the fire that raged through the inn, is affixed to the crumbling chimney, one of the few remaining parts of the structure that once made up the Shady Rest Inn.\nThe shield can be removed from the brick of the chimney.","rew":"Experience: 700","back":"Have you found evidence from the site of the Shady Rest Inn?","done":"Hm, I'm no expert with the construction of arms and armor. Their use, yes, but not their making.\nThis shield seems as ordinary as any, excepting the damage from the fire that engulfed the inn.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":29.6,"y":48.6,"n":"Black Shield","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":68.2,"y":48.6,"n":"Captain Garran Vimes","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"1173":{"id":1173,"t":"Challenge Overlord Mok'Morokk","lv":45,"min":38,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Defeat Mok'Morokk and report the news to Draz'Zilb in Brackenwall Village.","desc":"You dare challenge Overlord Mok'Morokk?\nHaw!\nMe crush tiny ‹race›!\nYou tell me when ready for good beating.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nFiendish Skiv Chillnail Splinter\nExperience: 4,850","back":"I thought you were going to attempt to drive Mok'Morokk out of the village. Instead you have come to me to chat?","done":"That cowardly fat mass Mok'Morokk fled like a scared child. You have done a great service, ‹name›.\nNow my people can appoint a new leader, one who will help us reclaim our old home once and for all.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":36.3,"y":31.4,"n":"Overlord Mok'Morokk","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":37.2,"y":33.1,"n":"Draz'Zilb","e":1}],"cats":["dustwallow-marsh"]},"6133":{"id":6133,"t":"The Ranger Lord's Behest","lv":60,"min":54,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the northern borders of the Eastern Plaguelands and recover the Quel'Thalas Registry. The item is somewhere in the Quel'Lithien lodge.\nYou must also slay 8 Rangers, 8 Pathstriders, and 8 Woodsmen.\nQuel'Thalas Registry Quel'Thalas Registry\nPathstrider slain : 0/ 8\nRanger slain : 0/ 8\nWoodsman slain : 0/ 8","desc":"The high elves of the Quel'Lithien lodge possesses something that belongs to me, ‹class›: A document detailing my life as a mortal.\nBefore you ask; no, you most certainly are not privy to such information. Just do as I tell you, worm: Recover the registry.\nAnd imbecile, be sure to leave as much strife and grief as possible in your wake. Leave them suffering...","rew":"Money: 90 0 gold, 90 silver, 0 copper Experience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Do not leave me waiting, ‹class›.","done":"I trust you did not read the registry. Not even you would do something that idiotic...","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":22.2,"y":63.5,"n":"Nathanos Blightcaller","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"91733":{"id":91733,"t":"Downstream","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect the Waterlogged Axe, Waterlogged Saw, and Waterlogged Toolbox that have washed downstream from Eastvale Logging Camp, then return to Ormin Pelford.\nWaterlogged Axe\nWaterlogged Saw\nWaterlogged Toolbox","desc":"I was bringing back a supply shipment from the trading post, but my wagon tipped over and the supplies fell in the river! Before I could catch them, they had already washed downstream.\nBetween the murlocs and wolves down there, I don't stand a chance of retrieving the supplies on my own. You seem like the hardy sort - do you think you could find them for me?","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 625\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Did you find the supplies?","done":"You look a bit damp, Urian. Sorry about that. But thank you for retrieving the supplies.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":76.4,"y":72,"n":"Ormin Pelford","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"7733":{"id":7733,"t":"Improved Quality","lv":48,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 10 Rage Scar Yeti Hides to Pratt McGrubben at Feathermoon Stronghold, Feralas.\n10 Rage Scar Yeti Hide Lurking Feral Scar , Ferocious Rage Scar 70 % , Elder Rage Scar 70 % , Rage Scar Yeti 70 %","desc":"I have a lead on an even BETTER source of hides, if that's even possible to believe! In the northern parts of Feralas - deep within Rage Scar Hold - are another throng of yetis. They're much tougher than the ones you dealt with before, so if you're up for a bigger challenge you'd best be on your toes!\nI would reward you handsomely for a stack of ten of their hides; bring them to me here, and we'll finish our business.","rew":"You will receive:\nPratt's Handcrafted Tunic\nMoney: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 4,400\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"If these Rage Scar yeti hides are anything like the quality displayed by their Feral Scar counterparts, they could very well be as resilient as thorium!\nImagine that!","done":"Excellent, excellent! These are going to work out incredibly well - I can already tell that they're going to be much harder when properly cured.\nThanks again for your help ‹name›. Here - please take one of my latest creations.","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":30.6,"y":42.7,"n":"Pratt McGrubben","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"533":{"id":533,"t":"Infiltration","lv":34,"min":29,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve information about Gol'dir's whereabouts for Krusk in Tarren Mill.\nSyndicate Missive Syndicate Thief 33 % , Syndicate Footpad 33 %","desc":"At last we begin to hear word and rumor, find evidence of Gol'dir's whereabouts. The humans have been moving him around, but we are narrowing down our search and focusing on the large Syndicate camp just north of here.\nGo there, ‹name›, and bring back whatever information you can get your hands on.","rew":"Money: 35 0 gold, 35 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,700\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"Have you found anything? I fear Gol'dir's prospects grow worse by the day...","done":"Finally, we know where Gol'dir is being held. The camp in question is not too far from here, and hopefully they will not be as well prepared as they were when they captured us the first time.\nHillsbrad Foothills Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":63.2,"y":20.7,"n":"Krusk","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"9333":{"id":9333,"t":"Argent Dawn Gloves","lv":60,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 50 instead of 55.","obj":"30 Necrotic Rune Bone Witch , Spirit of the Damned , Lumbering Horror , Shadow of Doom 38.4 % and 4 more","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGloves of Undead Cleansing Handwraps of Undead Slaying Handguards of Undead Slaying Gauntlets of Undead Slaying","back":"If you bring me thirty necrotic runes, I will give you your choice of hand protection in return. These should prove valuable in our fight against the undead Scourge.","done":"You've done well, ‹name›. Take your pick of hand protection in thanks for your efforts.\nUndercity Orgrimmar Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":65,"y":45.6,"n":"Argent Outfitter","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":52.2,"y":73.8,"n":"Argent Outfitter","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":42.1,"y":58.5,"n":"Argent Outfitter","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["invasion"]},"8933":{"id":8933,"t":"Just Compensation","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Lightforge Belt and a set of Lightforge Gauntlets to Deliana in Ironforge.\nLightforge Belt Rockwing Gargoyle 4.6 % , Rockwing Screecher 4.5 % , Crimson Gallant 4.3 % in Stratholme , Crimson Guardsman 1.8 % in Stratholme and 1 more\nLightforge Gauntlets Timmy the Cruel 0 %","desc":"You kept your word and brought the device built by Mux. I believe a reward is in order if I'm to keep you interested in saving my skin. Bring me the belt and set of gauntlets that you wish to upgrade. I promise the ones I give you in return will be far superior.","rew":"You will receive:\nSoulforge Belt Soulforge Gauntlets\nExperience: 9,950","back":"You're ready to perform the trade?","done":"You've kept your end of the bargain, I shall keep mine.\nJust remember that I'm holding on to the best pieces until your work is finished.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":58.1,"y":29.5,"n":"Deliana","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"2853":{"id":2853,"t":"Master of the Wild Leather","lv":45,"min":30,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Pratt's Letter to Telonis, the master leatherworker of Darnassus.\nPratt's Letter\nProvided: Pratt's Letter","desc":"Well ‹name›, you are the definition of diligence. There is one pattern left for Wild Leather armor; you've mastered the others. I won't require you to toil needlessly for the pattern. You've earned it outright, and then some... but I cannot give it to you myself. My teacher, the one who brought me into the craft, is the one who must reward you.\nTake this letter to Telonis; he teaches leatherworking in Darnassus. Show him the letter, and let him acknowledge you as an equal, as I do.","rew":"You will receive:\nPattern: Wild Leather Cloak\nExperience: 3,900","back":"Greetings, ‹race›... from your countenance I can tell you are a leatherworker as am I. Have you come to draw from my skills, or perhaps you have other business with me?","done":"Ah yes, Pratt sent you. Though he is a human, he reminds me of us night elves sometimes. His dedication and his talents with leather are impressive. For him to compliment you so in this letter, it is a sign of respect I acknowledge.\nI am aware that he has taught you the art of Wild Leather. Allow me to finish your training with this pattern. Make good use of it; few in the world know the secrets of Wild Leather cloaks.\nFeralas Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":30.6,"y":42.7,"n":"Pratt McGrubben","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":64.4,"y":21.5,"n":"Telonis","e":1}],"cats":["leatherworking"]},"86613":{"id":86613,"t":"Excavation tools","lv":18,"min":13,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Return 6 Excavation Tools to Magmar Fellhew.\nProvided: 6 Excavation Tools","desc":"The excavation's tools, left behind when the dwarves fled from the troggs, seem mostly untouched. Returning them to the excavators will surely aid their work.","rew":"Money: 10 0 gold, 10 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,350\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"We just, uh, need to adjust our dig site and we can get this whole thing back on track!","done":"Our tools!\nWhen the troggs overran the camp, we had to leave most of our tools behind. This'll be a big help once we get this invasion under control and can start working again!","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":65.8,"y":65.6,"n":"Prospector Ironband","e":1}],"cats":["loch-modan"]},"773":{"id":773,"t":"Rite of Wisdom","lv":10,"min":3,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to Red Rocks east of Thunder Bluff and speak with the Ancestral Spirit.","desc":"To gain acceptance amongst the elders of Thunder Bluff you must next complete the Rite of Wisdom.\nNow that you have passed the Rite of Vision, the ancestral spirits of Red Rocks will give you the blessing of our ancestors. Only those who have drunk from the Water of Seers can gain the blessing.\nTravel east of Thunder Bluff, to Red Rocks and seek out the Ancestral Spirit, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","done":"You have shown great diligence in your yearning to pass the Rites of the Earthmother, ‹name›.\nWe, the Ancestral Spirits, represent the mighty tauren who gave their lives bravely to found and protect our great city of Thunder Bluff. I hereby pass the duty of that protection over to you.\nYou have passed the Rite of Wisdom, young ‹class›. Enter Thunder Bluff with pride.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":34.3,"y":43.3,"n":"Seer Wiserunner","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":58.3,"y":30.7,"n":"Ancestral Spirit","e":1}],"cats":["mulgore"]},"9093":{"id":9093,"t":"Dreamwalker Wristguards","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Rayne at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Dreamwalker Wristguards if you bring her the following: 1 Desecrated Wristguards, 6 Wartorn Leather Scraps, 1 Arcane Crystal and 2 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Wristguards Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Grand Widow Faerlina 0 % in Naxxramas , Anub'Rekhan 0 % in Naxxramas\n6 Wartorn Leather Scrap Skeletal Steed 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Necro Knight Guardian 26.1 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 24.5 % in Naxxramas , Stoneskin Gargoyle 24.1 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\nArcane Crystal Hakkari Thorium Vein 5.8 % , Rich Thorium Vein 2.9 % , Ooze Covered Rich Thorium Vein 2.9 % , Small Thorium Vein 2.6 % and 4 more\n2 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"Many heroes fell in the last war and many continue to perish at the hands of the Scourge to this day. From the corpses of the fallen, the armor is stripped and taken back to Naxxramas to be used for unknown purposes.\nRecover the desecrated armor and wartorn armor scraps and supply to me the other material components I require and I will craft Dreamwalker armor.","rew":"You will receive:\nDreamwalker Wristguards\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"The material cost is high, but soon forgotten.","done":"Your Dreamwalker Wristguards are ready, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.4,"y":49.3,"n":"Rayne","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"9013":{"id":9013,"t":"Saving the Best for Last","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Give Mokvar your Helm of Valor and Breastplate of Valor.\nHelm of Valor Darkmaster Gandling 0 %\nBreastplate of Valor General Drakkisath 0 %","desc":"A truly amazing story, ‹name›! You have my thanks, and the heartfelt gratitude of all who were involved, I can assure you. Through your efforts we are delivered from the mistakes of our past.\nAs to your reward, I believe I have a few things that you have definitely earned and will truly enjoy.","rew":"You will receive:\nHelm of Heroism Breastplate of Heroism\nExperience: 1,650","back":"As per our deal, are you ready to hand over your Valor pieces in exchange for your new Helm and Breastplate of Heroism?","done":"I will truly miss you, ‹name›. There is a debt that I owe you, which I may never be able to repay.\nEnjoy your new head and chest armor. May it protect you for a long time to come, and help you to achieve even greater honor!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":34.9,"y":38.3,"n":"Mokvar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"7493":{"id":7493,"t":"The Journey Has Just Begun","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will learn: Onyxia Scale Cloak","done":"A dragon slayer and a seasoned leatherworker? You do not cease to astonish, hero. I am humbled.\nPlease accept what I am about to teach you. This knowledge will prove to be invaluable if you are to destroy what remains of the Black Dragonflight.\nCreate the cloak from the scales of the brood mother. It will protect you and your allies against the incendiary breath of the Lord of Blackrock... Nefarian.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":51.7,"y":75.5,"n":"Overlord Runthak","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"1653":{"id":1653,"t":"The Test of Righteousness","lv":21,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak to Jordan Stilwell in Ironforge","desc":"Actually, I have no doubt that Jordan himself would like to thank you, and seeing as I need a messenger to send word that his wife is safe, I think you'd be a perfect choice.\nJordan was to be a paladin of the Light before his dedication to his father's craft took him on another path--he's intimately familiar with our way of life and is considered among our most faithful.\nHe should still be in Ironforge--he likes to work outside the gates during the day, something about the cool mountain air.","rew":"Experience: 825","done":"Good day, ‹name›. The Light is with you, I trust?\nWhat's that? You were sent by Duthorian!? My wife, how is she? I knew there was going to be trouble if I left.\nPlease tell me she's... oh, thank goodness. I'm so glad that she's safe. The Defias were a threat long before these attacks, but now the King's advisors cannot deny it.\nWhat else did Duthorian have to say? You're the one that was sent to protect my wife? Then I thank you again, ‹name›. I couldn't think of a better test of valor than that.\nStormwind City Dun Morogh","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.5,"y":47.5,"n":"Duthorian Rall","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":52.5,"y":36.9,"n":"Jordan Stilwell","e":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"94773":{"id":94773,"t":"Divine grace","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","done":"You have done the Light a great service by becoming a shining example to those who travel in these dangerous lands and beyond. Please, accept this lesson as a thanks for all you've done.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":38.8,"y":26.4,"n":"High Priestess Laurena","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["priest"]},"8373":{"id":8373,"t":"The Power of Pine","lv":60,"min":25,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Use a Stink Bomb Cleaner to remove any Forsaken Stink Bomb that's been dropped on Southshore. Return to Sergeant Hartman in Southshore when you're done.\nProvided: Stink Bomb Cleaner","desc":"The thing I hate the most about Hallow's End are the stink bombs the Forsaken use on Southshore. Who knew that celebrating liberation would have to involve such a smelly mess?\nDuring Hallow's End, use this cleaner to remove any nasty stink bombs the Horde may drop here in the village. It uses the power of pine to fight funky smells.\nDo your part to keep Southshore clean, and I'll give you some Hallow's End treats I'm sure you'll enjoy. We have a deal?","rew":"You will receive:\n15 Hallow's End Pumpkin Treat\nExperience: 1,650\n+100 reputation with Alliance","done":"Ah, it almost smells better around here already. Almost.\nThanks to you, ‹name›, Southshore just might make it through another Hallow's End. Here's your treats, with my thanks! If you run out of candy, I think there's a gnome named Katrina Shimmerstar in Ironforge who can sell you more; she's only around during Hallow's End, I believe.","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":50,"y":57.5,"n":"Sergeant Hartman","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"1013":{"id":1013,"t":"The Book of Ur","lv":26,"min":16,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 5,600 experience instead of 2,100, 2.67 times as much. New rewards: Tattered Mittens. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a no","obj":"Bring the Book of Ur to Keeper Bel'dugur at the Apothecarium in the Undercity.\nThe Book of Ur The Book of Ur in Shadowfang Keep","desc":"‹name›, Shadowfang Keep holds a book, the Book of Ur, which would be much prized in my collection. Ur was a great mage of Dalaran before the coming of the Scourge, his studies in other worlds are of much value to ... certain parties among the Forsaken.\nEnter Shadowfang Keep and find the book. Bring it to me, and I will report your service to our Dark Lady...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nGrizzled Boots Steel-clasped Bracers Tattered Mittens\nNew in Forever: Tattered Mittens.\nExperience: 5,600\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Did you find the book, ‹name›?","done":"Very good. This book will add nicely to my collections of the workings of Ur. His knowledge was great, but his conscience held him from true power. And so when the Scourge came and his strength was tested, it failed.\nWe of the Forsaken cannot afford such weakness, if we are to survive...","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":53.7,"y":54.5,"n":"Keeper Bel'dugur","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shadowfang-keep"]},"3093":{"id":3093,"t":"Rune-Inscribed Note","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 40 experience instead of 50, 0.8 times as much.","obj":"Read the Rune-Inscribed Note and speak to Meela Dawnstrider in Camp Narache.\nRune-Inscribed Note\nProvided: Rune-Inscribed Note","desc":"Just a moment ago a messenger was looking for you, ‹name›. I believe she was sent by the shaman trainer Meela. If this note is from Meela, I wouldn't take long in reading it's contents.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"As quickly as water falls from the sky, here you are before me. I am pleased by your haste. It means you realize both the importance of our meeting and you being here. I am no leader, but I do understand the elements, and I can speak to the spirits of our people. I will teach you to do the same.","done":"We will meet many times in the days to come. Each time you will hopefully leave my company a little more powerful... a little more prepared. Like the Eternal Flame, your spirit will burn bright and hot.\nGo now, ‹name›. Go and test yourself. I will be here for you when you need.","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":44.5,"y":77.5,"n":"Grull Hawkwind","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":44.6,"y":76.6,"n":"Meela Dawnstrider","e":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"94373":{"id":94373,"t":"Call of earth","lv":4,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 2 Frostmane Bear Pendants to Teo Hammerstorm in Anvilmar.\n2 Iceclaw Bear Pendant","desc":"Aye, the time's come, young shaman. Ye've grown stout and sturdy, like the stone beneath our boots. Takin' up the shaman's path shows ye've got the wisdom o' the mountain, even before ye've proven yerself.. Ye've the grit of stone to walk the earth's path.\nBut to earn its favor, ye must face it proper. South o' here, the Frostmane trolls live in a cave.\nBring me two of their necklaces they wear--crafted from the Iceclaw bears. Then we'll speak more of yer future.","back":"Patience, lad, is the earth's finest virtue. It's seen mountains crumble and rivers carve valleys - slow and stubborn, like a true ‹race›. The earth calls to ye now, for trouble brews on the horizon. Return successful, and ye'll be one step closer to bein' whole.\nOthers may envy yer wisdom, but that's their burden to bear.","done":"Well done, lad. Ye've proven yerself ready. Earth's the bedrock of all things. Strength, stamina, patience. It'll shield ye, but only if ye show it proper respect. Even stone can shift if slighted. Learn its ways, and ye'll grow wiser than most. Never forget the secrets it shares.\nI'll craft ye a sapta now - accept it, and ye'll walk the true path.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.7,"y":66.1,"n":"Teo Hammerstorm","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8773":{"id":8773,"t":"Target: Hive'Zora Reavers","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Slay 30 Hive'Zora Reavers and report back to Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus. You must also bring Combat Task Briefing IV in order to complete this quest.\nCombat Task Briefing IV\nHive'Zora Reaver slain : 0/ 30\nProvided: Combat Task Briefing IV","desc":"Reinforcements have been called on to join the assault on Hive'Zora. You have been selected to target Hive'Zora reavers. Report back to Commander Mar'alith after completing your task.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Combat Badge\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You have something to tell me, ‹class›?","done":"I've heard good things about your part in the Hive'Zora attack. Keep up the good work and victory will soon be ours.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Commander Mar'alith","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"79093":{"id":79093,"t":"Rumi of gnomeregan the collected works","lv":20,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Rumi of Gnomeregan: The Collected Works","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 160","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nRumi of Gnomeregan: The Collected Works (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"1093":{"id":1093,"t":"Super Reaper 6000","lv":21,"min":16,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Get the Super Reaper 6000 Blueprints for Ziz Fizziks in the Stonetalon Mountains.\nSuper Reaper 6000 Blueprints Venture Co. Operator","desc":"Terrible what the Venture Company has done here, eh? What were they thinking? Goblin company hiring a gnome!\nLucky for me, Sputtervalve knows a genius when he sees one. Hired me just after I'd been kicked out!\nTells me they built some enormous woodcutting machine, and Sput' wants me to steal the plans for him. Unfortunately, Gerenzo--bloody gnome--wants me dead on sight... maybe you could steal the plans for me? You should be able to find them on one of their operators.","rew":"Experience: 1,650\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Did you find those plans? I'm eager to impress the new boss. Hopefully, once he's convinced of my loyalty--well, as much as he can be convinced... goblin's honor, you know?--he'll feel comfortable making use of my rather impressive genius.","done":"Hey, is that what I think it is? Great!\nNow, let's see. Ugh... how am I supposed to understand this stuff... can't figure out the way gnomes think. Lemme tell you, I'm surprised they could build the wheel, let alone those flying machines they like so much.","pins":[{"z":"Stonetalon Mountains","x":59,"y":62.6,"n":"Ziz Fizziks","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stonetalon-mountains"]},"373":{"id":373,"t":"The Unsent Letter","lv":22,"min":16,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 2,050 experience instead of 875, 2.34 times as much. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal quest.","obj":"Deliver the Letter to the City Architect to Baros Alexston in Stormwind.\nAn Unsent Letter Edwin VanCleef in The Deadmines\nProvided: An Unsent Letter","desc":"Searching Edwin VanCleef's person, you discover, among other things, an unsent letter. It is addressed to Baros Alexston, the City Architect of Stormwind, City Hall, Cathedral Square.\nIt appears to be recently written and sealed.","rew":"Money: 7 0 gold, 7 silver, 0 copper Experience: 2,050\n+50 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Yes? Is there something I can help you with?","done":"Edwin VanCleef, you say? I would as much expect a letter from my dead grandmother... So you've killed him then? Pardon me in saying, but I'm somewhat surprised. He was a peerless fighter in his younger years. Let's see what he finds the need to write to me about after so many years.\n<Baros peruses the letter.>\nEdwin... I see the years haven't changed you a bit, an idealist as ever, and a romantic. He doesn't care who he hurts, ‹name›. Revenge has consumed him. But then, I'm not sure I can blame him.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":57.7,"y":47.9,"n":"Baros Alexston","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"213":{"id":213,"t":"Hostile Takeover","lv":36,"min":31,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Retrieve 8 Tumbled Crystals and return them to Kebok in Booty Bay.\n8 Tumbled Crystal Venture Co. Geologist 52 %","desc":"He's done it this time! Bad enough that Gelriz's muscling out the moguls who were appointed by the trade princes, now he tries to cut in on the most notorious pirate!\nRevilgaz won't have it, and he's told me to take care of the problem in my own way.\nMy way? Theft. The Venture Co. geologists near Lake Nazferiti are deeply interested in those strange blue crystals they have been finding in the mines. Bring me samples of the stone from their geologists, I don't care what you have to do to get them.","rew":"You will receive:\nGemmed Gloves\nExperience: 2,800\n+100 reputation with Booty Bay\n-500 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"I need those stones, ‹name›. By whatever means necessary! Just do it, don't give me the details!\nIt's about results, ‹name›, nothing more, nothing less.","done":"Fascinating. That the crystals have been tumbled using this process can only indicate that they are planning to use them as some sort of fuel or other catalyst. I don't know much more than that. Samples will have to be dispatched to Head Chemist Gigglefont.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27,"y":77.1,"n":"Kebok","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"613":{"id":613,"t":"Cracking Maury's Foot","lv":44,"min":30,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. New rewards: Beggar's Leggings, Seadog's Battered Cuffs.","obj":"Bring Maury's Key to \"Sea Wolf\" Mackinley in Booty Bay.\nMaury's Key Mosh'Ogg Lord 40 % , Mosh'Ogg Butcher 30 % , Mosh'Ogg Shaman 24 % , Mosh'Ogg Mauler 22 % and 2 more","desc":"Curses! That swab Maury put a lock on his foot, and I can't open it! His loot's inside the foot, and that's what he owes me!\nWe need to find the key to open the lock. Maury was known to gamble with the Mosh'Ogg ogres, at their mound to the northeast. And he told me, when he was still alive, that the last time he went to the mound he was chased off after winning too much. Maybe the Ogres there have his key.\nBut if they do, you might have to kill a load of them to find the right one...","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nCollection Plate Beggar's Leggings Seadog's Battered Cuffs\nNew in Forever: Beggar's Leggings, Seadog's Battered Cuffs.\nExperience: 4,650\n+150 reputation with Booty Bay\n-750 reputation with Bloodsail Buccaneers","back":"Ahoy, ‹name›! Have you yet found Maury's Key?","done":"You found it! Thanks a million, ‹name›. You've been a big help to me!\nHere you go - you earned this!","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":27.8,"y":77.1,"n":"\"Sea Wolf\" MacKinley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8053":{"id":8053,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Freethinker's Armguards","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Level 60 instead of 61. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,500, 1.02 times as much.","obj":"Bring Jin'rokh the Breaker Primal Hakkari Bindings. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Friendly with the Zandalar Tribe.\nJin'rokh the Breaker is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Bindings\nReach 3000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"You are a heathen. Heathens have a place in the tribe. Heathens are freethinkers of Zandalar. Freethinkers do not fear oppression. Freethinkers die for what they believe in. We know you would die for what you believe in. This earns our acknowledgement. This earns you a chance to prove yourself further.\nWe must have the Paragons of Power. Go to Zul'Gurub. Kill the minions of Hakkar. Return when you have what I seek. Claim the first battle gear of a Zandalar freethinker.\nGo.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Freethinker's Armguards\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"You have returned? Do you have the Paragons of Power? Are you wasting my time?\nI hope not, heathen.","done":"You do much to honor us. Your hands drip with the blood of Hakkar's minions. You are a friend to the tribe.\nWear these bracers. They are the freethinker's armguards. This is what I mean about real power.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":15.3,"y":14.4,"n":"Jin'rokh the Breaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"933":{"id":933,"t":"Crown of the Earth","lv":9,"min":3,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Fill the Tourmaline Phial and bring it back to Corithras Moonrage in Dolanaar.\nFilled Tourmaline Phial\nProvided: Tourmaline Phial","desc":"There is another moonwell southeast of the entrance to Darnassus, on the shores of the Pools of Arlithrien. The Sentinels are having problems patrolling the area because of attacks and the growing ill-temperedness of the Gnarlpine furbolgs.\nBe wary as you seek out the well, and keep your weapons close at hand.","rew":"Experience: 775\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"At first the reports of crazed furbolg attacks were dismissed. Who could have thought that the peace-loving bear-men would turn to mindless rage? Yet another of the problems that plagues us here in our new home.","done":"Shan'do Stormrage never returned, and the druids were in disarray, and to this day we still do not know what became of him. With Malfurion missing, Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm took over the leadership of the druids, convincing the Circle of Ancients in Darkshore that it was time for our people to rebuild, and that it was time for our people to regain their immortality.\nWith the approval of the Circle, Staghelm and the most powerful druids grew Teldrassil, the new World Tree.","pins":[{"z":"Teldrassil","x":56.1,"y":61.7,"n":"Corithras Moonrage","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["teldrassil"]},"97253":{"id":97253,"t":"Parts and pieces","lv":14,"min":9,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 5 Handfuls of Complicated Parts from the upper pirate camp south of Ratchet, then return to Wrenix the Wretched in Ratchet.\n5 Handful of Complicated Parts","desc":"Hey, got a sec?\nSo, apparently, nobody I've sent to deal with the recent pirate problem has come back alive. After five or six attempts I thought, \"what if I sent a machine instead?\" Turns out, scimitars double as screwdrivers in a pinch, and before I could redirect it home, it was already in pieces and scattered across their camp!\nI need those parts back, and since this is a quick little retrieval mission, I'd wager your odds for survival are MUCH higher than the others. Whaddya say?","rew":"You will receive:\nScuffed Shipping Crate\nMoney: 6 0 gold, 6 silver, 0 copper Experience: 975","back":"Not another word out of you until your pockets are jingling with metal!","done":"Whooooa! Nice one, pal! You saved me from another one of Gagsprocket's unbearable lectures on the cost of metal. More importantly, I can jump right into building my next prototype.\nUhhh, I didn't have a reward planned... Do you like boxes?","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":63,"y":36.4,"n":"Wrenix the Wretched","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"853":{"id":853,"t":"Apothecary Zamah","lv":15,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the Rendered Spores to Apothecary Zamah in Thunder Bluff, before the time limit is up.\nRendered Spores\nProvided: Rendered Spores","desc":"I have rendered the spores you gave me into an emulsion. I must now send it to my associate, Apothecary Zamah. If you were to carry this to her, she can offer you something from our stores of alchemical goods.\nShe is in the Pools of Vision, a cave beneath the shamans of Thunder Bluff. The path to this cave is well hidden, but you may find it on the Spirit Rise bluff.\nDo hurry. This emulsion will maintain its potency for only a short time, and must be resealed and processed before then.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\n4 Elixir of Minor Fortitude 4 Elixir of Minor Agility 3 Minor Rejuvenation Potion 2 Swiftness Potion\nYou will also receive:\nCauldron Stirrer\nExperience: 800\n+75 reputation with Undercity","back":"You have something from Apothecary Helbrim?","done":"Ah, the spores from the Barrens that Helbrim was gathering. He garnered your aid in delivering them? Good.\nAnd the emulsion is still potent, so you must have wasted no time in the delivery. Well done, ‹class›.\nThe Barrens Thunder Bluff","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":51.4,"y":30.2,"n":"Apothecary Helbrim","s":1},{"z":"Thunder Bluff","x":22.8,"y":20.9,"n":"Apothecary Zamah","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"2933":{"id":2933,"t":"Venom Bottles","lv":43,"min":40,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring a Venom Bottle to an apothecary in Tarren Mill.\nVenom Bottle\nProvided: Venom Bottle","desc":"These bottles hold a vile, green venom.\nConsidering the number of bottles in this village, the Witherbarks must deem it very important. Perhaps an apothecary in nearby Tarren Mill would like a sample.","rew":"Experience: 3,600\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"Hello, gentle ‹class›. The day has been long and not a single experiment successful...I hope you bring good news to me.","done":"Ah, and what is this? It appears to be venom... from some arachnoid creature I deem. And where did you get it?\nThe Hinterlands Hillsbrad Foothills","pins":[{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":23.5,"y":58.8,"n":"Venom Bottle","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":23.2,"y":58.6,"n":"Venom Bottle","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":23.2,"y":58.7,"n":"Venom Bottle","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":31.5,"y":57.7,"n":"Venom Bottle","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":31.6,"y":57.7,"n":"Venom Bottle","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":31.6,"y":57.8,"n":"Venom Bottle","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":23,"y":57.7,"n":"Venom Bottle","s":1},{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":61.4,"y":19.1,"n":"Apothecary Lydon","e":1}],"cats":["the-hinterlands"]},"4293":{"id":4293,"t":"A Sample of Slime...","lv":52,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Gather Felwood Slime Samples from any of the slimes in Felwood. Then, using the Testing Equipment next to Chemist Fuely in Undercity, see which of your samples are the most corrupt. Bring 5 of the Corrupted Felwood Samples you find to Chemist Fuely.\n5 Corrupted Felwood Sample","desc":"Felwood is a forest far north of the Barrens, even farther than Ashenvale. There, slimes are found all around pools of water blessed by the touch of Fel. The Scourge decimated the area with attacks of Infernals and other demonic magics--the slimes supposedly crept up through the earth during these attacks.\nGather samples of Felwood slimes and we will use the testing equipment next to me to create a control group for our tests against other samples you gather.","rew":"Money: 60 0 gold, 60 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,100\n+100 reputation with Undercity","back":"I will need at least five corrupted samples for our control group, ‹name›. Continue to gather Felwood slime samples until you're able to give me that which we'll need. The Lady Sylvanas decrees it...","done":"Ah, excellent. These samples will do nicely. I thank you for your help.\nOnce we've gathered all the samples of slimes, we'll be able to determine more. I am beginning to suspect that Lady Sylvanas' hunch was not only correct, but more insightful than even she could have predicted. These samples are very interesting. Just seeing how they've reacted with my compounds... hmm, yes, we'll definitely need to investigate further.\nUndercity Felwood Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":47.5,"y":73.3,"n":"Chemist Fuely","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"7813":{"id":7813,"t":"A Donation of Wool","lv":60,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Wool Cloth Farrin Daris 66.7 % , Adam Lind 62.1 % , Mountaineer Langarr 57.1 % , Protector Leick 47.6 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 650\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"We are currently accepting donations for wool cloth. A donation of sixty pieces of wool cloth will net you full recognition by the Undercity for your generous actions. Our stores are such on wool that we would only need sixty pieces from you total; we should be able to acquire enough from others in the realm to support our drive.\nIf you have the sixty pieces of wool cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Undercity","x":71.7,"y":29.2,"n":"Ralston Farnsley","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["undercity"]},"5093":{"id":5093,"t":"A Call to Arms: The Plaguelands!","lv":50,"min":50,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out High Executor Derrington. His base camp is located at the Bulwark, east of Tirisfal Glade and the Undercity.","desc":"Heroes of the realm, hear me - the Horde calls upon you for swift action!\nA call to arms has been issued for all able bodied individuals to take up arms against the Scourge! Rumors fly of new threats rising from the ruins of the Eastern Kingdoms. They loom to the east of the Undercity, in the northern reaches of the lands now known as the Plaguelands!\nHeroes of the realm - seek out High Executor Derrington, who has set up his base camp at the Bulwark, east of Tirisfal Glade!","rew":"Experience: 470\n+10 reputation with Undercity","done":"Welcome to the Plaguelands, hero. This is one of the most dangerous frontiers in Azeroth, with the looming threat of the Scourge to our east, and then even further still eastward from there. I am glad to hear that the call of duty and service to the Horde did not fall on deaf ears with you!\nIf you are ready to get your hands dirty, then there is plenty for willing and able heroes to do here on the edge of the Plaguelands.\nOrgrimmar Tirisfal Glades","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48.2,"y":66.1,"n":"Warcaller Gorlach","s":1},{"z":"Tirisfal Glades","x":83.1,"y":68.9,"n":"High Executor Derrington","e":1}],"cats":["western-plaguelands"]},"53":{"id":53,"t":"Sweet Amber","lv":44,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Grimbooze Thunderbrew a bundle of Charred Oak.\nBundle of Charred Oak The Charred Oak","desc":"Mellifluous liquid clear as a baby's tears\nTurns a lovely deep amber over the years\nBut before we proceed to get lit to the hilt\nA barrel of charred oak must be built.","rew":"You will receive:\nThunderbrew's Boot Flask\nExperience: 5,600","back":"Sure, I'll sing it again for you, friend!\nMellifluous liquid clear as a baby's tears\nTurns a lovely deep amber over the years\nBut before we proceed to get lit to the hilt\nA barrel of charred oak must be built.","done":"Aged in the barrel, filtered through coal\nIt passes your lips and right through your soul.\nSo lets us drink now, a toast to you\nAnd me while we're at it, Grimbooze Thunderbrew!\nWestfall Searing Gorge","pins":[{"z":"Westfall","x":44.6,"y":80.3,"n":"Grimbooze Thunderbrew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["westfall"]},"293":{"id":293,"t":"Cleansing the Eye","lv":30,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Archbishop Benedictus the Cursed Eye of Paleth. Benedictus is in the Cathedral of Light, in the city of Stormwind.\nCursed Eye of Paleth\nProvided: Cursed Eye of Paleth","desc":"I can't lift the curse from the Eye of Paleth. The Eyes were crafted by Human Priests, so you'll have to go to Stormwind to find someone who can help you. Speak with Archbishop Benedictus. He is head of the Cathedral of Light in Stormwind. He can help.\nI hope, for your sake.","rew":"You will receive:\nEye of Paleth\nExperience: 2,450\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"What is that orb you have? It looks...soiled.","done":"An Eye of Paleth. But this one has seen much sorrow...it must have been witness to a terrible, terrible tragedy.\nLet me cleanse it, for the Eyes were created to shine bright, and their powers can be quite dangerous if tainted like this one.\nWetlands Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":10.6,"y":60.6,"n":"Glorin Steelbrow","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":50.3,"y":45.5,"n":"Archbishop Benedictus","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"98293":{"id":98293,"t":"Forced disarmament","lv":30,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Collect 30 Dragonmaw Armaments in Dragonmaw Retreat, then bring them to Captain Stoutfist in Menethil Keep.\n30 Dragonmaw Armaments","desc":"The Dragonmaw are stockpiling all manner of weaponry. It would be wise to relieve them of these before more soldiers can be armed.\nCaptain Stoutfist in Menethil Keep would surely be interested in these.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":58.8,"y":45.1,"n":"Dragonmaw Armaments","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":9.8,"y":57.4,"n":"Captain Stoutfist","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"5253":{"id":5253,"t":"The Crystal of Zin-Malor","lv":58,"min":53,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Crystal of Zin-Malor to Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus.\nCrystal of Zin-Malor\nProvided: Crystal of Zin-Malor","desc":"Quite impressive, ‹name›.\nThe crystal of Zin-Malor can never be returned to the temple which, as you know, lies in ruin. But I believe that your effort to undo the evil of the past should not go unrewarded.\nSeek out Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm in Darnassus, and bring the crystal to him, ‹name›. It should be in the hands of those that will not abuse its power. From the looks of it, only a handful of the strongest magic users would be able to control such a power.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nTurquoise Sash Plow Wood Spaulders Emerald Mist Gauntlets\nExperience: 6,200\n+100 reputation with Alliance","back":"Yes, ‹race›?","done":"I have heard of the Crystal of Zin-Malor; the user of the crystal becomes capable of incredible arcane power, but only if truly worthy. I am impressed that you not only recovered the crystal, but you also realize your own limits, and did not attempt to use the crystal yourself.\nThank you for bringing it to me, ‹name›. We will keep it safe, and may the cursed sprits that once guarded the shattered crystal finally be at peace.\nWinterspring Darnassus","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":52,"y":30.4,"n":"Wynd Nightchaser","s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":34.8,"y":9.3,"n":"Arch Druid Fandral Staghelm","e":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"92693":{"id":92693,"t":"Standing our ground","lv":9,"min":5,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Aamelia Windfield when you are ready to confront the bandit leader.\nSpeak with Aamelia Windfield\nFollow Aamelia and make your final stand","desc":"You've done a lot to give us a fighting chance. Even if we die today, we'll at least know we gave it our best shot.\nThis is your last chance, stranger. If you want to head back to Valanaar and live another day, I wouldn't blame you.\nOn the other hand, if you really have a thing for lost causes just let me know when you are ready to go. We'll walk out there with our heads held high and whatever happens, happens.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Red Delicious Stormapple\nExperience: 200","back":"There's not enough stormapples in skywall to repay you for this.","done":"I... can't believe it's over. I need to stop and calm myself before my heart leaps right out of my chest.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":46.6,"y":81.8,"n":"Aamelia Windfield","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]}});